quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  11,109,"So, (O listener) do not be in doubt regarding (the idols) these (pagans) worship. They worship nothing except what their forefathers worshipped before. We will most surely pay them their portion (of punishment) in full, without any reduction."
  11,110,"Indeed, We gave the Book to Musa (Moses), but differences arose regarding it. And had not a Word gone forth from your Lord, the matter would have been decided between them. Indeed, they are in confounding doubt about it."
  11,111,"Your Lord will indeed recompense them all for their deeds in full. Indeed, He is All-Aware of what they do."
  11,112,"So remain steadfast, just as you have been commanded, along with those who have returned (to Allah) with you, and do not transgress. Indeed, He is All-Seeing of whatever you do."
  11,113,"And (O people!) do not incline towards the wrongdoers, lest the Fire should touch you. And you will have no protectors besides Allah. Then you shall not be helped."
  11,114,"And establish the prayer at both ends of the day (i.e. dawn and sunset) and during the early hours of the night. Indeed, good deeds wipe out evil deeds (i.e. virtue effaces vice). That is a reminder for the mindful."
  11,115,"And be patient, for surely Allah does not waste the reward of the virtuously excellent."
  11,116,"So why were there not among the generations before you, those possessing the right understanding, who could have forbidden corruption on the earth? (There was none) except a few of those whom We saved among them (from the punishment). And the wrongdoers pursued only the (worldly) luxuries they had been given, and they were guilty."
  11,117,And your Lord would never have destroyed the towns unjustly while their people were reforming (themselves).
